<Layout
	title="League Rules"
	description="Current League Rules"
	pubDate={new Date('June 23 2026')}
>

	<p>
		Need a rundown of the rules of the league? You came to the right spot.
	</p>
<h3>Draft Rules</h3>
	<p>
		The draft rules are somewhat convoluted, especially as they have evolved over time. The following rules are the current rules, not the historical rules.
	</p>
<h4>Summer Draft</h4>
	<ul>
		<li>The Summer draft is three rounds of six picks.</li>
		<li>The draft is in the inverse order of the end of year standings.</li>
		<li>The draft is non-serpentine. All rounds have the same order.</li>
		<li>Any player who has played in a regular season or postseason NBA game is ineligible for the draft.</li>
		<li>Any player who has been drafted and subsequently cut is ineligible for the draft.</li>
		<li>Picks can be appended onto the end of the draft for any reason.</li>
	</ul>
<h4>Winter Draft</h4>
	<ul>
		<li>The Winter draft is two rounds of six picks.</li>
		<li>The draft is in the inverse order of the standings at the time of the draft.</li>
		<li>The draft is serpentine, so the order of the recond round is the reversal of the first.</li>
		<li>Players who have played in NBA games but have not exhausted their rookie limits are eligible for the draft.</li>
	</ul>
<h3>Roster Rules</h3>
	<ul>
		<li>Teams are allowed up to 23 players.</li>
		<li>The scoring positions are as follows: <ul>
			<li>PG</li>
			<li>SG</li>
			<li>G x2</li>
			<li>SF</li>
			<li>PF</li>
			<li>F x2</li>
			<li>C x2</li>
			<li>F/C</li>
			<li>Util x4</li>
		</ul></li>
		<li>Incomplete rosters are allowed.</li>
	</ul>
<h3>Scoring Rules</h3>
	Starting in 2026, the TCML is a 10 cat league. The following 9 categories are in play every year:
	<ul>
		<li>Points</li>
		<li>Rebounds</li>
		<li>Assists</li>
		<li>Three Pointers Made</li>
		<li>Field Goal Percentage</li>
		<li>Free Throw Percentage</li>
		<li>Steals</li>
		<li>Blocks</li>
		<li>Turnovers (lower wins)</li>
	</ul>
	In addition to that, a 10th category will be decided by the lowest placing team the prior year. The category for the 2026 season is <b>Double-Doubles</b>.
<h3>Playoffs</h3>
	Six teams make the playoffs, which are decided by regular season record. The top two teams get a first round bye.